# M3: walking off a ledge is NOT a jump.
#
# SMB1 reports Player_State = 2 when the floor stops being under you
# (PlayerBGCollision's SetFallS path), which the adapter maps to
# air_cause = FELL. grounded = 0 alone cannot distinguish this from a launched
# jump, and guessing from the pad is wrong because the adapter samples input a
# frame before SMB1 acts on it -- so if this regresses, walking off a ledge
# launches you upward.

stick_x 80
frames 20
expect_state RUN

# Off the edge of a tall ledge, so there is room to fall.
note host-walks-us-off-a-ledge
pos_y 2000
host_fall
frames 1
expect_state FALL

# Still falling ten frames later. A mistaken jump would have gone up and come
# back; a mistaken kneebend would read KNEEBEND here. FALL rather than
# FALL_AERIAL also proves no jump was consumed on the way off the ledge.
frames 10
expect_state FALL

# Landed, back to ground locomotion with the stick still held.
frames 60
expect_state WALK_FAST
